From ef007a70a09f555ba4e90199b9977dde43a7294d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 10:22:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] droidcamsrc: set recording-hint when switching to video mode

QCOM's HAL1 only sets up the camera's recording stream once it has been told
a recording session is coming. Without recording-hint=true the camera accepts
startRecording() and the vendor encoder is even created and configured -
OMX.qcom.video.encoder.avc at the negotiated size, with mm-camera logging an
ENCODER hw_stream - but no CAMERA_MSG_VIDEO_FRAME is ever delivered. Android's
CameraSource then sits in 'Timed out waiting for incoming camera video frames'
and 'Waiting on an available memory base timed out. Dropping a recording
frame.', the recorder's data callback never fires, vidsrc pushes nothing and
the recording comes out empty. Seen on tissot (msm8953, Halium 9); the
parameter is advertised as recording-hint=false there.

Set it from apply_mode_settings() rather than next to the recorder: the
parameter has to be in place before the recorder is created, and mode changes
run through apply_mode_settings() with SET_AND_APPLY, well before
start-capture. It is only touched when the HAL advertises the key, so devices
that do not know it are left exactly as they were, and it is cleared again on
the way back to image mode so stills do not keep the video tuning.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrc.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrc.c b/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrc.c
index c6f9a4c..abfd8b3 100644
--- a/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrc.c
+++ b/gst/droidcamsrc/gstdroidcamsrc.c
@@ -2372,6 +2372,25 @@ gst_droidcamsrc_apply_mode_settings (GstDroidCamSrc * src,
     gst_droidcamsrc_dev_enable_face_detection (src->dev, TRUE);
   }
 
+  /* recording hint
+   *
+   * QCOM's HAL1 only sets up the camera's recording stream when it has been
+   * told a recording session is coming. Without recording-hint=true,
+   * startRecording() is accepted and the vendor encoder is even created, but
+   * no CAMERA_MSG_VIDEO_FRAME ever arrives: Android's CameraSource sits in
+   * "Timed out waiting for incoming camera video frames", vidsrc pushes
+   * nothing and the recording ends up empty.
+   *
+   * The parameter has to be in place before the recorder is created, which is
+   * why it is set here - mode changes run through apply_mode_settings() with
+   * SET_AND_APPLY, well before start-capture - rather than next to the
+   * recorder itself. Only touch it when the HAL advertises it, so devices
+   * that do not know the parameter are left exactly as they were. */
+  if (gst_droidcamsrc_params_get_string (src->dev->params, "recording-hint")) {
+    gst_droidcamsrc_params_set_string (src->dev->params, "recording-hint",
+        src->mode == MODE_VIDEO ? "true" : "false");
+  }
+
   /* image noise reduction */
   gst_droidcamsrc_apply_quirk (src, "image-noise-reduction",
       src->image_noise_reduction);
